    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to introduce to the market No. 48 The Woods, a well presented four-bedroomed semi-detached home, ideally situated within the popular The Woods development. This home offers a lovely balance of living and bedroom accommodation that has been beautifully finished and maintained.\n\nThe ground floor comprises an entrance hall, living room, guest w.c., utility room, and a spacious open-plan kitchen/dining area with a sliding glass door opening onto the rear garden. The first floor accommodates three well-proportioned double bedrooms, a single bedroom, family bathroom and hot press storage. \n\nExternally, the property benefits from allocated parking to the front. To the rear, a south-westerly facing garden enjoys a sunny aspect and is accessed directly from the kitchen/dining area. Designed for low maintenance, the garden features a level lawn, a Barna shed, and is fully enclosed by timber fencing, providing a good degree of privacy.\n\nGlounthaune is an extremely convenient location offering residents the calmness of country living while being a 15-minute drive to Cork city centre. Glounthaune railway station is only a short walk and a regional bus service links the village to Cork city, Cobh and Midleton is right on your doorstep. Close by is the Jack Lynch Tunnel with easy access to the main routes to Dublin and Waterford. \n\nThe property is also convenient to schools, shopping centres and Little Island, offering a wide variety of coffee shops and retail outlets to include Eastgate Retail Park and The Radisson Blu Hotel & Leisure Centre.\n\nTo fully appreciate this home, arrange a viewing today!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.65m x 1.89m\nThis bright and welcoming entrance hall features tiled flooring and provides access to all ground floor accommodation.\n\nLiving Room - 4.76m x 4.07m\nA spacious living room overlooking the front drive, featuring venetian blinds and finished with laminate wood flooring.\n\nW.C. - 1.44m x 1.48m\nGuest W.C. comprising a two-piece suite with tiled flooring.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 3.57m x 6.05m\nLocated to the rear of the property, this bright open-plan kitchen and dining area is well fitted with a range of floor and eye-level units complemented by white marble countertops, a breakfast bar, and a selection of premium kitchen appliances. The dining area overlooks the rear garden through sliding glass doors and features tiled flooring throughout.\n\nUtility Room - 1.57m x 2.68\nLocated just off the kitchen, the utility room features tiled flooring and is plumbed for both a washing machine and dryer. It also provides convenient direct access to the side of the home.\n\nLanding - \nThe carpeted landing provides access to the four bedrooms and main bathroom on the first floor, with a Stira staircase offering access to the attic.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.28m x 3.87m\nPositioned to the front of the property, this spacious double bedroom features a Juliet balcony overlooking the front driveway, built-in wardrobes, and the added benefit of a private en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - 1.96m x 1.78m\nEn-suite comprising a three-piece suite with tiled flooring, part-tiled walls, and a shower fitting.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.69m x 3.89m\nThis double bedroom is located to the rear of the property and features carpet flooring and a window overlooking the rear garden.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.06m x 2.4m\nThis double bedroom is positioned to the front of the property and features laminate wood flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.51m x 3.00m\nSingle bedroom positioned to the rear of the home with wood flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.95m x 1.97m\nFully tiled main bathroom featuring a three-piece bath suite. Benefits from quality bathroom fittings including a heated towel rail and fitted storage units.\n\n"
      },
